<!--enter p.1-->
    <p.1 id="Para-317">3.A typical regulation in New Jersey specifies that one of the purposes of CPS
is to <q>[p]reserve and strengthen family life</q>: New Jersey Administrative Code
10:133C-2.3(a)(2); N.J.S.A. 30:4C-1(a). This principle means that family ties
must be encouraged and preserved to the greatest extent possible under the
circumstances of a given case.
</p.1>
    <!--end of p1 paragraph-->


<!--enter p.1-->
    <p.1 id="Para-318">4.See transcript of decision, June 22, 2001, p. 14.
