<!--enter p.1-->
    <p.1 id="Para-458">43.Rand, <q>Munchausen Syndrome by Proxy: A Complex Type of Emotional Abuse
Responsible for Some False Allegations of Child Abuse in Divorce,</q> p. 135. It
should be noted that Rand’s <q>contemporary</q> version of MSBP differed sharply
from the syndrome as originally defined. Rand was willing to apply the MSBP
label even when mothers had not induced any symptoms in their children, nor
exposed them to invasive or dangerous procedures, whereas these were formerly
both important elements of the syndrome.
</p.1>
    <!--end of p1 paragraph-->


